.TH tujson n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tujson
.PP
Small dependency\-free JSON helpers in pure Tcl.
.SS API
.CS
package require tclutils::tujson

::tclutils::tujson::quote text
::tclutils::tujson::escape text
::tclutils::tujson::minify json
::tclutils::tujson::pretty json ?-indent string?
::tclutils::tujson::validate json
::tclutils::tujson::parse json
::tclutils::tujson::fromJson json
.CE
.PP
\fBparse\fR maps JSON objects to Tcl dictionaries and JSON arrays to Tcl lists. Strings are returned as Tcl strings, numbers as their original numeric text, \fBtrue\fR as \fB1\fR, \fBfalse\fR as \fB0\fR, and \fBnull\fR as the empty string.
.SS Example
.CS
set d [::tclutils::tujson::parse {{"name":"Gregor","items":[1,2]}}]
dict get $d name      ;# Gregor
dict get $d items     ;# 1 2
.CE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tujson.tcl validate data.json
tclsh bin/tujson.tcl minify data.json
tclsh bin/tujson.tcl pretty data.json
tclsh bin/tujson.tcl parse data.json
.CE
.SS Scope
.PP
The parser supports standard JSON values: objects, arrays, strings, numbers, \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR, and \fBnull\fR, including common string escapes and Unicode escapes. It intentionally does not implement JSON5, comments, trailing commas, JSONPath, or a streaming parser.
.SS parseTyped
.PP
\fB::tclutils::tujson::parseTyped json\fR parses JSON into a \fItyped\fR tree, unlike \fBparse\fR/\fBfromJson\fR which return native Tcl values and lose the object/array/scalar distinction. Each node is a two\-element list \fB{type value}\fR:
.TS
l l.
type	value
\fBobject\fR	dict mapping key \-> typed node (insertion order preserved)
\fBarray\fR	list of typed nodes
\fBstring\fR	the unescaped string
\fBnumber\fR	the number in its source spelling
\fBboolean\fR	\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR
\fBnull\fR	empty string
.TE
.CS
% ::tclutils::tujson::parseTyped {{"tags":["x"],"n":1}}
object {tags {array {{string x}}} n {number 1}}
.CE
.SS "Encoding: toJson"
.PP
\fBtoJson\fR is the inverse of \fBparseTyped\fR; it serialises a \fItyped value\fR back to JSON text, so \fBtoJson [parseTyped $json]\fR round\-trips \fB$json\fR.
.PP
A typed value is the tagged form \fBparseTyped\fR returns:
.TS
l l.
JSON	Typed value
string \fB"x"\fR	\fB{string x}\fR
number \fB1\fR	\fB{number 1}\fR
\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR	\fB{boolean true}\fR
\fBnull\fR	\fB{null {}}\fR
object	\fB{object {key {typed} ...}}\fR
array	\fB{array {{typed} ...}}\fR
.TE
.PP
Build values by hand with the constructors \fBstr\fR, \fBnum\fR, \fBbool\fR, \fBnull\fR, \fBobj\fR, \fBarr\fR:
.CS
package require tclutils::tujson
set doc [tujson::obj [list \
    name [tujson::str "Alice"] \
    age  [tujson::num 30] \
    ok   [tujson::bool 1] \
    tags [tujson::arr [list [tujson::str x] [tujson::str y]]] \
    note [tujson::null]]]

tujson::toJson $doc
# {"name":"Alice","age":30,"ok":true,"tags":["x","y"],"note":null}

tujson::toJson $doc -indent 2
# pretty-printed with 2 spaces per level
.CE
.PP
\fB\-indent N\fR (N > 0) pretty\-prints; the default (0) is compact. Strings are escaped via \fBquote\fR; numbers are validated; unknown tags raise \fB{TCLUTILS TUJSON TYPE}\fR.
